      equipment: 'Score-keeping paper and pen.',
      dealing: "Deal all 13 cards to each player (one at a time, face-down). After looking at their hands, players pass 3 cards to an opponent. Passing direction rotates each round: Left, Right, Across, then No Pass (a 'hold' round). This 4-round cycle repeats.",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. PASSING: After the deal, each player selects 3 cards to pass to an opponent (direction rotates: Left, Right, Across, None). All passes are simultaneous.\n2. OPENING LEAD: The player with the 2 of Clubs leads it to the first trick.\n3. FOLLOWING SUIT: Players must follow the suit led if possible. If unable to follow suit, any card may be played (except penalty cards on the first trick).\n4. WINNING TRICKS: The highest card of the suit led wins the trick. There is no trump suit. The trick winner leads the next trick.\n5. BREAKING HEARTS: Hearts cannot be led until a heart has been played ('discarded') on a previous trick, or the player has nothing but hearts remaining.\n6. FIRST TRICK RESTRICTION: No penalty cards (hearts or Queen of Spades) may be played on the first trick.\n7. SCORING: After all 13 tricks are played, each player counts penalty points in their captured tricks. Each heart = 1 point, Queen of Spades = 13 points. Maximum penalty per round = 26 points.\n8. SHOOT THE MOON: If one player captures ALL 13 hearts AND the Queen of Spades, they score 0 and every other player scores 26 points.\n9. GAME END: Play continues across rounds until a player reaches 100 cumulative points. The player with the lowest score at that point wins.",
